        "id": 55402,
        "name": "Chaosmancer",
        "username": "Chaosmancer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-31T05:27:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I have never played blind, I'm also still a relatively new player. I almost never get the chance to play with others, and playing a solo game with 3 heroes, a villain, and an environment you've never seen before... I couldn't handle it, I can barely keep things straight knowing the cards sometimes (I once played an entire game with Spite skipping his play phase, because his end of turn effect of playing a card made me forget he had a play phase... It's hard running everything at once late at night)</p><p>Also, I just love seeing everything. I want to see how everything works so I can start getting an idea of what would happen. I still never figure out strategies until much later though, there is no way to remember all the cards you see when reading through 6+ decks of cards.</p>",
